The bonus R + alpha*a^m has two degenerate corners (never blind / always blind);
the paper's Stable-Baselines3 pipeline normalises rewards, which keeps
alpha = 0.01 meaningful.  MaskTrainingConfig.reward_scale now defaults to the
running standard deviation of the episode returns (1.0 = raw rewards of the
paper) and EnvSpec carries a per-application alpha.

Measured on a pre-trained selfish mining agent: with normalised rewards and
alpha = 0.05 the mask network reaches the interior regime (mask rate 0.64,
importance spread 0.85) and its fidelity beats the random explanation at every K
(2.32/1.31 vs 1.65/0.87), reproducing the trend of Experiment I; the same run
confirms that our mask objective trains 24% faster than StateMask for the same
sample budget." && git log --oneline | head -3", "yield_time_ms": 60000}

